<!-- PROBLEM / GOAL -->

<section>

<h2>The Problem / Goal</h2>

<p>

Analyze how Last Day on Earth combines survival,
exploration, resource gathering, crafting and
base building into a connected gameplay experience.

</p>

<p>

The objective of this case study is to understand
how the game creates player motivation through
resource scarcity, progression, environmental danger
and long-term survival goals.

</p>

<p>

<b>My Role:</b>

Game Design Analysis, Gameplay Systems Analysis,
UI/UX Evaluation, Progression Analysis
and Design Improvement Concepts.

</p>

</section>



<!-- CORE GAMEPLAY LOOP -->

<section>

<h2>Core Gameplay Loop</h2>

<p>

The gameplay revolves around collecting resources,
surviving dangerous locations, crafting useful items
and gradually strengthening the player's base.

</p>

<div class="grid">

<div class="card">

<b>01. Explore</b>

Travel to different locations
and discover resources.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>02. Gather</b>

Collect wood, stone, food,
materials and equipment.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>03. Survive</b>

Manage health, hunger, thirst
and dangerous encounters.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>04. Craft</b>

Convert collected materials
into useful survival equipment.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>05. Build</b>

Expand and improve your
survival base.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>06. Progress</b>

Unlock new equipment,
locations and challenges.

</div>

</div>

</section>



