<!-- IMPROVEMENTS -->

<section>

<h2>Gameplay Analysis & Improvements</h2>

<p>

The following are design opportunities identified
through analysis. They are proposed improvements,
not verified problems reported by the developer.

</p>


<div class="grid">


<div class="card">

<b>Inventory Organization</b>

Improve item categorization
and make resource management
easier to navigate.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>New Player Guidance</b>

Provide clearer early-game guidance
for crafting, gathering
and survival priorities.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>Crafting Clarity</b>

Make missing crafting materials
and required resources
easier to identify.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>Combat Feedback</b>

Improve visual feedback
for attacks, damage
and enemy interactions.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>Progression Clarity</b>

Make long-term crafting
and base-building goals
easier to understand.

</div>


<div class="card">

<b>Resource Planning</b>

Improve information about
resource requirements
before starting an expedition.

</div>


</div>

</section>



<!-- PLAYTEST -->

<section>

<h2>Gameplay Analysis & Iteration</h2>

<p>

Instead of presenting unverified playtest results,
this case study focuses on analyzing the original
gameplay systems and identifying possible
design improvements.

</p>


<ul>

<li>
<strong>Inventory Experience:</strong>
Analyzed how limited storage affects
resource collection and item prioritization.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Crafting Experience:</strong>
Reviewed how crafting requirements
connect resource gathering with progression.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Survival Management:</strong>
Examined how hunger, thirst and health
influence exploration decisions.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Player Progression:</strong>
Analyzed how crafting unlocks,
equipment and base upgrades
create long-term objectives.
</li>

<li>
<strong>Exploration:</strong>
Reviewed the relationship between
location danger, resource rewards
and player preparation.
</li>

</ul>

</section>



